                {
                  "id": "6904f9f6-63cd-4933-9b6b-d4b762620131",
                  "text": "[陈述] Set",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "102f0a17-2552-4f66-a013-8375d2df254a",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 陈述\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Mathlib.Data.Set.Defs`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nType u → Type u\n```\n\n**文档**\nA set is a collection of elements of some type `α`.\n\nAlthough `Set` is defined as `α → Prop`, this is an implementation detail which should not be\nrelied on. Instead, `Set.ofPred` (also written `{x | p x}`) and membership of a set (`∈`) should be\nused to convert between sets and predicates.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "陈述",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f8fbff",
                    "color": "#1e3a8a",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#93c5fd"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ce2fd5ca-2483-4867-8a43-2574589094dc",
                  "text": "[证明] Set.ext",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "102f0a17-2552-4f66-a013-8375d2df254a",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** theorem\n\n**模块** `Mathlib.Data.Set.Defs`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {α : Type u} {a b : Set α}, (∀ (x : α), x ∈ a ↔ x ∈ b) → a = b\n```\n\n**文档**\n（无 docstring）",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "theorem"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
